00:29:52.923 --> 00:29:53.756
- Right.
- Okay.

00:29:53.756 --> 00:29:55.090
- And if you understand
the emotions, like,

00:29:55.090 --> 00:29:57.550
the trigger for voice goes
through the limbic system

00:29:57.550 --> 00:29:59.240
which is part of where
our emotion comes from,

00:29:59.240 --> 00:30:00.303
hypothalamus--
- The trigger for voice.

00:30:00.303 --> 00:30:01.630
- The trigger, like the--

00:30:01.630 --> 00:30:03.180
- Oh, the trigger for voice.

00:30:03.180 --> 00:30:04.626
- Nerves firing for the voice.

00:30:04.626 --> 00:30:05.480
- So, the trigger for the interaction

00:30:05.480 --> 00:30:06.712
of voice with another person.

00:30:06.712 --> 00:30:08.210
- Yes, it runs through the limbic system,

00:30:08.210 --> 00:30:11.780
and so emotion then can
be encoded on the voice

00:30:11.780 --> 00:30:12.613
because it's running through that.

00:30:12.613 --> 00:30:13.446
- Whoa!

00:30:13.446 --> 00:30:16.880
- Which is why when you
were talking to someone

00:30:16.880 --> 00:30:19.070
and you say, I'm terribly sorry,

00:30:19.070 --> 00:30:22.050
but I need you to move this along,

00:30:22.050 --> 00:30:24.544
and they say, calm down, and you're like,

00:30:24.544 --> 00:30:26.693
I am not upset!

00:30:28.760 --> 00:30:30.910
- You a lyin' mofo.
- Right, exactly.

00:30:30.910 --> 00:30:31.980
- It's hard to hide.

00:30:31.980 --> 00:30:33.300
- It's hard to hide!
- Because it's there.

00:30:33.300 --> 00:30:35.610
Which is what makes a performer so unique

00:30:35.610 --> 00:30:37.510
because they're actually taking a signal,

00:30:37.510 --> 00:30:38.410
you know what happens to your voice

00:30:38.410 --> 00:30:39.600
