00:35:42.290 --> 00:35:45.580
Chuck hosts a sports spinoff of StarTalk

00:35:45.580 --> 00:35:48.120
called Playing With Science and all manner

00:35:48.120 --> 00:35:50.300
of these topics come up, but now we have

00:35:50.300 --> 00:35:52.340
an analog in a whole other field.

00:35:52.340 --> 00:35:54.130
You are fixing your performance.

00:35:54.130 --> 00:35:56.598
- Yeah, well--
- So people will applaud,

00:35:56.598 --> 00:35:58.120
rather than--
- Voice doping.

00:35:58.120 --> 00:35:59.740
- Voice doping, yes.
- That's cool.

00:35:59.740 --> 00:36:01.620
- Doping brings, I mean, doping in sports

00:36:01.620 --> 00:36:04.260
brings you to the ability
to do it, though, live.

00:36:04.260 --> 00:36:05.680
Whereas Auto-Tune doesn't.

00:36:05.680 --> 00:36:08.600
Auto-Tune puts it on some
kind of digital format

00:36:08.600 --> 00:36:11.360
and so I think what Kelly
said is right on the money.

00:36:11.360 --> 00:36:14.131
I think if you can't do
it live, what's the point?

00:36:14.131 --> 00:36:14.964
Because you're trying to commune.

00:36:14.964 --> 00:36:16.000
Most people perform because they're trying

00:36:16.000 --> 00:36:16.833
to commune with people.

00:36:16.833 --> 00:36:18.990
- Yeah, but if you
can't perform any longer

00:36:18.990 --> 00:36:20.810
and Auto-Tune helps you hit that note,

00:36:20.810 --> 00:36:23.568
then that's, to me,
sounds just like doping.

00:36:23.568 --> 00:36:24.910
- It does.

00:36:24.910 --> 00:36:27.476
- Okay.
(all laugh)

00:36:27.476 --> 00:36:28.309
Well, there you have
it, there you have it!

00:36:28.309 --> 00:36:29.410
There you go!

00:36:29.410 --> 00:36:32.796
I was ready for a fight,
but nope, that's it!

00:36:32.796 --> 00:36:33.629
There it is!

00:36:33.629 --> 00:36:35.503
- I agree with you, Dr. Tyson.

00:36:38.431 --> 00:36:39.400
